    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107370" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεργήρ-ως</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ων</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>exceedingly old, of
				extreme age,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.622
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				47.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				27.9
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὑ.</span>”
				<i>extreme old age,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					79
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <i>past the age of service,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PGiss.
				59iv 14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>: prob. proparox.: sts. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέργηρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			in codd. (so in <u>Gloss.</u>); pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέργηροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Vett.Val.
					350.19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
